From: Nfrastack <code@nfrastack.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: notification settings cannot be saved when server lacks default push rules

Bug: Saving any notification setting 404s with M_NOT_FOUND
("Push rule not found") on homeservers whose push-ruleset lacks
server-default rules such as .m.rule.contains_display_name,
.m.rule.contains_user_name or .m.rule.roomnotif. reconcile always emits
those as "updated" entries, and applyChanges only ever calls
setPushRuleEnabled/setPushRuleActions, which require the rule to already
exist - so every save fails and the whole reconciliation is rejected.

Fix: on M_NOT_FOUND, (re)create the missing rule with addPushRule from
its spec-stable template (conditions/pattern; the failing rule IDs are
all long-frozen defaults), then apply the requested enabled/actions on
top, so the created rule converges to exactly what the settings UI asked
for. Rules without a known template still throw as before.

